  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 1.5.5, package-lock.json says 1.5.4, package-lock.json packages[\"\"] says 1.5.4.",
        "  make version of ncmake bumps info.xml, composer.json and package.json and re-syncs package-lock.json in one step, so they cannot drift apart. ncmake's lint-version workflow fails a push or a pull request on exactly this drift. The App Store and the server read info.xml, npm and composer read their own manifest. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying more than one version number, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ],
      "covers": [
        "lint-version/version-drift"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "screenshot-not-image",
      "lines": [
        "A screenshot of appinfo/info.xml is not served as an image:",
        "  <screenshot> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nextcloud/IntraVox/main/screenshots/calendarwidget-intro.gif: application/octet-stream",
        "  The App Store shows the bytes behind the URL, so it needs the image itself; a github.com/.../blob/... URL is the page around it, raw.githubusercontent.com serves the file."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0 (package.json, composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 32 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  AGPL-3.0 (package.json, composer.json) is a deprecated SPDX id, replaced because it does not say whether -only or -or-later is meant.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is intravox, the checkout directory is IntraVox.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 32 to 33; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 32 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "No Node version is stated: no engines.node, no .nvmrc, and no node-version in the installed workflows.",
        "  Whoever builds the app uses whatever Node they have, and a build that works on one machine is then not evidence for the next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: PHPUnit (phpunit.xml).",
        " No ESLint configuration: nothing checks the frontend sources, so a wrong import is found by the build or not at all.",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "script-names",
      "lines": [
        "In package.json, build:dev is a development build, which it names dev.",
        "  Under those names a contributor finds them in every app without reading package.json."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "13 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @mdi/svg, @nextcloud/paths, @tiptap/extension-blockquote, @tiptap/extension-code, @tiptap/extension-code-block, @tiptap/extension-details, @tiptap/extension-horizontal-rule, @tiptap/extension-task-item, and 5 more.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 434 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
